.TH PORTSYNC 1 "2026-09-07" "emerald" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portsync \- synchronize Emerald port repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portsync
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portsync
fetches configured ports repositories into the local ports tree. Repositories are shallow-fetched from the configured branch (\fBmain\fR by default) and checked out into their destination directories.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -p, --prune
Prune local repository data after synchronization.
.TP
.B -r, --reset
Reset repository state before synchronization.
.TP
.B -s, --source REPO...
Synchronize only the named repositories. The option consumes repository names until the next option.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
portsync
portsync --source main
portsync -s main custom
portsync -r -s main
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when all selected repositories synchronize; non-zero when a repository cannot be created, fetched, or checked out.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR emerald.repo (5),
.BR emerald (1)
